Guided Exercise: Troubleshoot Containers and Pods
Objective
In this lab you learn to:
•	Investigate why a pod fails to start
•	Check logs and events
•	Fix the container image
•	Copy files into a pod
•	Access the pod database
•	Use port forwarding
The application used is MySQL.
________________________________________
1. Prepare the Lab Environment
Run the lab preparation command.
lab start pods-troubleshooting
This ensures:
•	cluster is running
•	required files are available
________________________________________
2. Login to OpenShift
Login as developer user.
oc login -u developer -p developer \
https://api.ocp4.example.com:6443
Expected output:
Login successful
________________________________________
3. Create Project
Create a new project for the exercise.
oc new-project pods-troubleshooting
Output:
Now using project "pods-troubleshooting"
________________________________________
4. Create MySQL Pod
Create a pod called mysql-server.
Image used:
registry.ocp4.example.com:8443/rhel9/mysql-80:1228
Command:
oc run mysql-server \
--image registry.ocp4.example.com:8443/rhel9/mysql-80:1228 \
--env MYSQL_USER=redhat \
--env MYSQL_PASSWORD=redhat123 \
--env MYSQL_DATABASE=world
Environment variables:
Variable	Value
MYSQL_USER	redhat
MYSQL_PASSWORD	redhat123
MYSQL_DATABASE	world
________________________________________
5. Check Pod Status
Check pod status.
oc get pods
Output:
NAME           READY   STATUS             RESTARTS
mysql-server   0/1     ImagePullBackoff   0
Meaning:
Pod cannot pull the container image
________________________________________
6. Check Logs
Check pod logs.
oc logs mysql-server
Output:
container is waiting to start:
trying and failing to pull image
Problem confirmed:
Image cannot be pulled
________________________________________
7. Check Cluster Events
Check events to find exact error.
oc get events
Important error message:
Failed to pull image
manifest unknown
Meaning:
Image tag does not exist
________________________________________
8. Check Available Image Tags
Login to container registry.
skopeo login registry.ocp4.example.com:8443
Credentials:
username: developer
password: developer
________________________________________
Inspect repository tags.
skopeo inspect \
docker://registry.ocp4.example.com:8443/rhel9/mysql-80
Available tags:
1
1-224
1-228
1-237
latest
Problem discovered:
Tag 1228 does NOT exist
Correct tag:
1-228
________________________________________
9. Fix Pod Image
Edit the pod configuration.
oc edit pod/mysql-server
Change:
image: registry.ocp4.example.com:8443/rhel9/mysql-80:1228
To:
image: registry.ocp4.example.com:8443/rhel9/mysql-80:1-228
Save and exit.
________________________________________
10. Verify Pod Status
Check again.
oc get pods
Output:
NAME           READY   STATUS
mysql-server   1/1     Running
Meaning:
Pod successfully started
________________________________________
11. Copy SQL File Into Pod
Copy database script.
oc cp ~/DO180/labs/pods-troubleshooting/world_x.sql \
mysql-server:/tmp/
File location inside pod:
/tmp/world_x.sql
________________________________________
12. Verify File in Pod
Check file using exec.
oc exec -it pod/mysql-server -- ls -la /tmp/
Expected file:
world_x.sql
________________________________________
13. Access Pod Shell
Open shell inside pod.
oc rsh mysql-server
Prompt becomes:
sh-5.1$
________________________________________
14. Login to MySQL
Run:
mysql -u redhat -p
Password:
redhat123
________________________________________
15. Select Database
USE world;
Output:
Database changed
________________________________________
16. Import SQL Script
Run:
SOURCE /tmp/world_x.sql
This creates tables and inserts data.
________________________________________
17. Verify Tables
Run:
SHOW TABLES;
Output:
city
country
countryinfo
countrylanguage
Exit:
exit
exit
________________________________________
18. Configure Port Forwarding
Forward MySQL port.
oc port-forward mysql-server 3306:3306
Output:
Forwarding from 127.0.0.1:3306 -> 3306
Meaning:
localhost:3306 → mysql pod
________________________________________
19. Connect From Local Machine
Open new terminal.
Connect using MySQL client.
mysql -u redhat -p -h 127.0.0.1 -P 3306
Password:
redhat123
________________________________________
20. Verify Database
Select database:
USE world;
List tables:
SHOW TABLES;
Count records:
SELECT COUNT(*) FROM country;
Output:
239
Meaning:
Database imported successfully
Exit:
exit
________________________________________
21. Stop Port Forwarding
Return to first terminal.
Press:
Ctrl + C
This stops the connection.
________________________________________
22. Finish the Lab
Clean resources.
lab finish pods-troubleshooting
This prevents conflicts with future labs.
________________________________________
Complete Troubleshooting Workflow
Typical debugging steps:
1 oc get pods
2 oc logs pod
3 oc get events
4 fix image/configuration
5 oc edit pod
6 oc cp files
7 oc rsh pod
8 oc port-forward
________________________________________
Key Problem in This Lab
Root cause:
Invalid container image tag
Wrong:
mysql-80:1228
Correct:
mysql-80:1-228
________________________________________
✅ Final Result
•	Pod successfully started
•	Database initialized
•	Tables imported
•	Data verified through port forwarding

